Dear Elena,

As promised in Newport, a short update ahead of our formal letter:

1. Re-manufacture of the 9.2 km section is on track. Conductor stranding is complete,
   CCV line 2 is at 61 % of the insulated length. No deviations so far.
2. The load-out date for export cable 2 remains 12 March 2027. We have provisionally
   reserved the cable lay vessel for an August 2027 slot as per your resequenced plan.
3. On CO-010 we can accept the vessel and engineering costs (approx. EUR 4.1 m of the
   EUR 6.8 m). We do not accept the standby element at this stage and would like to
   discuss it together with the LD start date.

Our formal letter will follow on Monday. Happy to set up a call with our CEO and
Dr. Okafor if you think that helps.

Kind regards,
Richard

